msgid "Hobbywing DroneCAN ESC"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hobbywing-dronecan-esc.rst:11
#: d9fb032b4a6b43ec8d8cdc2f05db9470
msgid "Hobbywing ESCs with CAN interfaces (`including these <https://www.hobbywing.com/en/products?id=46>`__) support DroneCAN which allows the autopilot to control the ESC/motor via CAN and also retrieve the individual rpm, voltage, current and temperature."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hobbywing-dronecan-esc.rst:13
#: 20f715da99d34465a42611bd3403ffdb
msgid "be sure that the CAN version of the ESC is being ordered. Contact Hobbywing if there is doubt. Some ESCs may require special ordering to get CAN interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hobbywing-dronecan-esc.rst:15
#: 41a755e10f35442bb3e2d23e8e49d460
msgid "The contents of this page were verified using a `Hobbywing X6 Plus (6218-150KV CW motor) <https://www.hobbywingdirect.com/collections/xrotor-x8-series/products/xrotor-pro-x6-series>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hobbywing-dronecan-esc.rst:17
#: fb2d03461080489c9ae388aee030f0a2
msgid "Some images courtesy of hobbywing.com"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hobbywing-dronecan-esc.rst:20
#: 8c1bd4724f1d4654b896a5408e855017
msgid "Connection and Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hobbywing-dronecan-esc.rst:22
#: ec075847cdf1450e935a77ab3bfbc976
msgid "Connect the ESCs (perhaps using a 4-pin I2C splitter) to the autopilot's CAN1 (or CAN2) port."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hobbywing-dronecan-esc.rst:24
#: 7d362b87ba71480ca3a080fd42c74d57
msgid "the CAN_H wire color varies from red to gray depending on product"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hobbywing-dronecan-esc.rst:30
#: 9c3fbe0ed4614272a7d109ff63fdac23
msgid "Connect to the autopilot with a ground station and set the following parameters and then reboot the autopilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hobbywing-dronecan-esc.rst:32
#: 78714d939026447d94b8e2c54474f141
msgid "Set :ref:`CAN_P1_DRIVER<CAN_P1_DRIVER>` to 1 (First Driver)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hobbywing-dronecan-esc.rst:33
#: caeb648f81cf4cc98255ecc10f513120
msgid "Set :ref:`CAN_D1_PROTOCOL<CAN_D1_PROTOCOL>` to 1 (DroneCAN)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hobbywing-dronecan-esc.rst:34
#: 07df96c5baa446f58ef7822ecd2efcbc
msgid "Set :ref:`CAN_D1_UC_ESC_BM<CAN_D1_UC_ESC_BM>` to configure which servo outputs are transmitted over CAN.  For most quadcopters this should be set to 15 to send outputs 1-4 to DroneCAN."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hobbywing-dronecan-esc.rst:39
#: 152a5360d7a341339cbc7942b58ee0f1
msgid "Modify :ref:`CAN_D1_UC_OPTION<CAN_D1_UC_OPTION>` so that \"Hobbywing ESC\" is checked (or directly set to 128)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hobbywing-dronecan-esc.rst:45
#: cefdbbbef8954a07a8c286aaa3f3c6e2
msgid "Configuring the ESCs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hobbywing-dronecan-esc.rst:47
#: 9b5f7d04d51e4c3583cb79e0a00023cf
msgid "By default the ESCs come from the factory with an incorrect baudrate (500,000 instead of 1,000,000) and all IDs are set to 1 (the first motor).  The instructions below show how to configure the ESCs to use the correct baudrate and individual ID for each ESC."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hobbywing-dronecan-esc.rst:49
#: 01fa72d4956e43518eb431ca64e137ee
msgid "You may initially test that the ESCs can be spun in their factory configuration by doing the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hobbywing-dronecan-esc.rst:51
#: 775522c3ee494c3ba24fd8a08cb9ad43
msgid "Disconnect any other DroneCAN devices from the autopilot's CAN1 port"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hobbywing-dronecan-esc.rst:52
#: 9e5712bc432d497892a016f39ebdf3a0
msgid "Connect to the autopilot and set :ref:`CAN_P1_BITRATE<CAN_P1_BITRATE>` to 500,000"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hobbywing-dronecan-esc.rst:53
#: 06b71ef8132a490aaa966f9efd20310f
msgid "Reboot the autopilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hobbywing-dronecan-esc.rst:54
#: c0cfe5ddb34240b5bbc0f9474faccb80
msgid "Power on the ESCs, they should stop beeping"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hobbywing-dronecan-esc.rst:55
#: 2c0e5ec6db66413bb362cad4f8444698
msgid "Use Mission Planner's Setup, Optional Hardware, Motor Test page's \"Test All Motors\" and all motors should spin"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hobbywing-dronecan-esc.rst:57
#: 60ad92cd7c8243f892cb0e66d80ac301
msgid "Next correct the configuration of each ESC:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hobbywing-dronecan-esc.rst:59
#: 864ba49b5c3147aab7a983195fe91962
msgid "Ensure the autopilot's :ref:`CAN_P1_BITRATE<CAN_P1_BITRATE>` param is set to 500,000 (reboot the autopilot if modified)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hobbywing-dronecan-esc.rst:60
#: 5280ede7b3f34adeb8d2a5dccab4b488
msgid "Download and install a the :ref:`DroneCAN Gui<common-uavcan-gui>` (version 1.2.25 or higher)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hobbywing-dronecan-esc.rst:61
#: 875019aab39b4a08a7ad6a06c4bafd0e
msgid "Determine the autopilot's MAVLink or SLCAN COM port.  More details can be found on the :ref:`DroneCAN GUI page<common-uavcan-gui>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hobbywing-dronecan-esc.rst:62
#: 35b2b6305b6c45db98e2ff00369e7133
msgid "Open the DroneCAN GUI"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hobbywing-dronecan-esc.rst:64
#: c813060c61e14e1680cd9aafb7f241a5
msgid "Connect to the MAVLink or SLCAN COM port"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hobbywing-dronecan-esc.rst:65
#: 18f2d1da1a6843c993064b9bc026a882
msgid "Push the check button beside the \"Set local node ID\" field"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hobbywing-dronecan-esc.rst:66
#: 632358c84f644c96be41fa3a4f121671
msgid "Select Panels, Hobbywing ESC Panel"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hobbywing-dronecan-esc.rst:67
#: cc5da480cb1249419a950b80461633cf
msgid "From the top table select an ESC"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hobbywing-dronecan-esc.rst:68
#: c1a33539706346c6b107012169e03656
msgid "Set the Baudrate to 1,000,000"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hobbywing-dronecan-esc.rst:69
#: fafc177dfd7443498c8e79d087ce119b
msgid "Set ThrottleID and NodeID to the ESC number.  This ESC number corresponds to the autopilot's servo/PWM output port number"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hobbywing-dronecan-esc.rst:70
#: 39ba6d536f9947aebd9c4d1ab261c12b
msgid "The values in the top table should update within a few seconds"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hobbywing-dronecan-esc.rst:71
#: 09d6cbd39dec4a60a71fc6f70c277500
msgid "Optionally you may wish to set Msg1Rate (rate at which RPM is sent to autopilot) and/or Msg2Rate (voltage, current temp).  Note Msg1Rate must be greater than Msg2Rate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hobbywing-dronecan-esc.rst:72
#: 3835a071aad44ae396c9ed4e1bfd5cc0
msgid "Repeat for each ESC"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hobbywing-dronecan-esc.rst:77
#: 148415b2204043c186d152dd78757f38
msgid "Connect to the autopilot and set :ref:`CAN_P1_BITRATE<CAN_P1_BITRATE>` back to 1,000,000"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hobbywing-dronecan-esc.rst:80
#: d301811f6d934b2e93a1d038b1a7a5b0
msgid "Testing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hobbywing-dronecan-esc.rst:82
#: 0b5a82fcce5847349547d40cecb535c0
msgid "Once connected the ESC's RPM, voltage, current and temperature will be visible in the ground station and recorded in the onboard logs.  The image below shows where the data appears on Mission Planner's Status screen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-hobbywing-dronecan-esc.rst:88
#: 57d2326c58b4470cb9b5f7c754aee84e
msgid "Test each motor spins properly using Mission Planner's Setup, Optional Hardware, Motor Test pages"
msgstr ""

